[h1]Immersive Chefs[/h1]

Immersive Chefs makes cooking physical: cooks use tools, reusable tableware, prepared ingredients and assistants, then somebody washes the dishes. Material, quality, sanitation, skill and temperature matter.

[b]For RimWorld 1.6.[/b]

[h1]Mechanics[/h1]

[list]
[*][b]Stuff-aware kitchenware[/b] - Material and quality affect cleanliness, comfort, speed and cooking; lead and uranium can slowly add toxic buildup.
[*][b]Physical meal service[/b] - Meals use real cookware, plates and cutlery that return dirty. Handheld, baby and animal foods stay excluded.
[*][b]Dishwashing and sanitation[/b] - Wash by hand or machine; dirty ware increases food-poisoning risk. Filters, forbidding and interruption recovery are supported.
[*][b]Ingredient preparation[/b] - Fast-rotting prepared portions retain their ingredients and prep quality, then accelerate final cooking.
[*][b]Cooperative cooking[/b] - Linked, manned stations add speed and quality only while assistants and the lead cook work together.
[*][b]Culinary quality[/b] - Ingredients, prep, skill, tools and teamwork create quality-driven mood and food-poisoning outcomes.
[*][b]Meal temperature and reheating[/b] - Meals cool naturally and can be microwaved at a quality cost; Thermodynamics can take full ownership.
[*][b]Dining standards[/b] - Expectations and Royalty titles demand better meals and settings; emergency eating never deadlocks.
[*][b]Travel, guests, children and patient feeding[/b] - Caravans conserve dishes, guests respect ownership, children dine, and nurses carry cutlery.
[*][b]Nutrient paste[/b] - Pawns bring plates to dispensers, which can also create anonymous low-quality prepared paste.
[*][b]Trade and world-generated meals[/b] - Ware has low thematic trader stock; eligible trader/visitor/raider meals gain cheap plates, but legacy unplated meals stay unplated.
[/list]

[h1]Things[/h1]

[list]
[*][b]Primitive stone cookware set[/b] - Cheap rough pots, pans, lids and utensils from any eligible stone Stuff.
[*][b]Cookware set[/b] - Reusable medieval or modern sets from eligible metals, plastics and registered materials.
[*][b]Glitterworld cookware set[/b] - Rare high-performance, self-cleaning trade/quest cookware.
[*][b]Plate and adobe plate[/b] - Reusable primitive-to-luxury service ware; adobe is an optional fixed-material variant.
[*][b]Cutlery setting[/b] - One reusable fork, spoon and knife setting.
[*][b]Chef's knife set[/b] - Quality-bearing utility-slot cooking tools that do not replace weapons.
[*][b]Prepared ingredients[/b] - Fast-rotting portions that remember ingredients and preparation quality.
[/list]

[h1]Buildings and research[/h1]

[list]
[*][b]Dishwasher[/b] - A powered 16-setting machine whose cycles pause safely.
[*][b]Industrial dishwasher[/b] - A faster 64-setting Professional Kitchens machine.
[*][b]Ingredient prep station[/b] - A workbench for prepared-ingredient bills.
[*][b]Sauce station[/b] - Linked assistance for sauce and finishing work.
[*][b]Meat station[/b] - Linked assistance for meat preparation.
[*][b]Vegetable station[/b] - Linked assistance for vegetable work.
[*][b]Pastry station[/b] - Linked assistance for pastry and desserts.
[*][b]Microwave[/b] - A table/workbench appliance for reheating, omitted with Thermodynamics.
[/list]

[h1]Required Mods[/h1]

[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2009463077][b]Harmony[/b][/url] - The only required third-party mod. Load it before Core.
[/list]

[h1]Optional Mods[/h1]

Integrations are package-gated and absent-safe; a changed upstream API disables only that adapter.

[list]
[*][b]Royalty[/b] - Title expectations demand progressively finer meals, plates and cutlery.
[*][b]Biotech[/b] - Independent children dine normally; toddler/baby feeding remains excluded.
[*][b]Processor Framework[/b] - Runs dishwasher processing while exact ware and sanitation survive.
[*][b]Expanded Materials - Metals[/b] - Adds suitable metals to recipes and material effects.
[*][b]Expanded Materials - Masonry[/b] - Enables adobe plates and broad stone recipes.
[*][b]Simply Sublime ABS Polymer[/b] - Correctly registers ABS as plastic.
[*][b]Dubs Bad Hygiene[/b] - Adds supplied plumbing, water debit, sink priority and fallbacks.
[*][b]Gastronomy[/b] - With Cash Register, waiters bring cutlery, reheat, serve and clear exact dishes.
[*][b]Hospitality[/b] - Guests prefer colony ware, then their own, without ownership drift.
[*][b]Common Sense[/b] - Diners/nurses take used settings to washing.
[*][b]Pick Up And Haul[/b] - Pawns batch nearby dishes and use its tracked unload workflow.
[*][b]Cook for Yourself[/b] - One-off self/dependent jobs use the full culinary lifecycle.
[*][b]Variety Matters[/b] - Preserves authoritative ingredient-variety provenance.
[*][b]Vanilla Food Variety Expanded[/b] - Preserves provenance for supported food content.
[*][b]Dynamic Meal Texture Replacer[/b] - Retains ingredient graphics through plating and dining.
[*][b]Food Texture Variety[/b] - Core loads before main; matching VCE add-ons retain selected textures and saved indices.
[*][b]Vanilla Expanded Framework[/b] - Preserves framework-owned building/recipe behavior used by supported add-ons.
[*][b]Vanilla Textures Expanded - Variations[/b] - With Vanilla Expanded Framework, adds stat-neutral building/ware variations.
[*][b]Vanilla Nutrient Paste Expanded[/b] - With Vanilla Expanded Framework, preserves taps/pipes while adding plates.
[*][b]Adaptive Meal Bill[/b] - Applies ware after upstream chooses the concrete recipe.
[*][b]Meals on Wheels Continued[/b] - Plates travel with borrowed/shuttle meals until eaten.
[*][b]Replimat / Replimat Meals[/b] - Replimat loads before its Meals add-on; plates precede dispensing and feedstock stays native.
[*][b]Vanilla Cooking Expanded[/b] - With Vanilla Expanded Framework (and Fishing for Sushi), classifies Cooking, Bakery, Haute, Stews and Sushi.
[*][b]Fried Meals[/b] - With Harmony and Vanilla Expanded Framework, classifies full meals but excludes ingredients/snacks.
[*][b]Fast Meals[/b] - Preserves deliberately fast recipe work.
[*][b]Prioritize Meals over Preserved Foods[/b] - Preserves upstream food ordering.
[*][b]RimCuisine 2[/b] - Processor Framework loads before Core, then modules; meals are classified but preservation, drinks and drugs stay excluded.
[*][b]Meal Printer[/b] - Plates printed meals, preserves feedstock and excludes NutriBars.
[*][b]RimFridge[/b] - Preserves complete meal/ware state in upstream storage.
[*][b]Adaptive Storage Framework[/b] - Remains passive and preserves complete serving state in upstream holders.
[*][b]SBZ Fridge[/b] - Loads after Adaptive Storage Framework and coexists passively with its cooling and holders.
[*][b]Overcooked Meals[/b] - Transfers culinary/ware state once to replacements.
[*][b]No Vanilla Meals[/b] - Handles removed vanilla Defs and registered replacements safely.
[*][b]Thermodynamics - Hot Meals[/b] - Exclusively owns temperature, heating and microwave behavior.
[/list]

[h1]Localization[/h1]

Complete English, German, Spanish, French, Simplified Chinese and Russian catalogs are included, plus ware, fallback, integration and visual settings.

[h1]Scope[/h1]

Food preservation, food waste, unsupported ceramics/porcelain and pre-release migration are outside this release.

[h1]AI disclosure[/h1]

Pre-generated AI tools assisted with programming, testing, documentation, localization and some artwork. The shipped outputs were reviewed, edited and validated during development; the mod does not generate AI content while RimWorld is running.
